    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d633">

                <pb facs="0647" n="531" sameAs="frus:frus1915/pg531"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 838.51/438.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Minister Blanchard to the Secretary of
                    State</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegrams.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Port au Prince</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-11-29T22:00:00-04:49">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">November 29, 1915—10 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Recommended in conference with the Admiral that $100,000 out of funds in hand be
                    paid to Haitian Government. The Government has asked for $48,000 in the case of
                    the Central Railroad of Haiti, and all will be paid tomorrow. A general modus
                    vivendi is being signed. Think most advisable loan $1,500,000 be arranged
                    immediately after the departure of commission, and so recommend.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Blanchard.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
